---
import ContentPage from '../components/ContentPage.astro';
import type { FaqItem } from '../lib/jsonld';

const faqs: FaqItem[] = [
	{
		question: 'Do you store or upload my JSON?',
		answer:
			'No. Every JSON document you paste, type, or open is processed entirely in your browser using client-side JavaScript. It is never uploaded, transmitted, logged, or stored on any server. You can verify this in your browser dev-tools network tab, or by using the tools fully offline.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Do you use cookies or trackers?',
		answer:
			'We do not use tracking or advertising cookies, and we do not run third-party analytics that profile you. The site stores only small preferences (such as your theme choice) in your browser’s local storage, which never leaves your device.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Can I use JSON Beam offline?',
		answer:
			'Yes. Because all processing happens client-side, the tools keep working with no network connection once the page has loaded. Working offline is the strongest guarantee that your data stays with you.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Will you ever add analytics or ads?',
		answer:
			'We may add privacy-respecting, aggregate analytics or non-tracking ads in future to keep the tools free. If we do, we will update this policy first — and the content you process will still never be transmitted, sold, or shared.',
	},
];
---

<ContentPage
	slug="/privacy"
	title="Privacy Policy — JSON Beam"
	description="JSON Beam's privacy policy: your JSON is processed entirely in your browser and never uploaded, logged, or shared. Read exactly how we handle data."
	breadcrumbLabel="Privacy Policy"
	h1="Privacy policy."
	intro="Privacy is not a feature we added — it is how JSON Beam is built. Everything runs in your browser, so the data you work with never leaves your device."
	lastUpdated="June 22, 2026"
	faqs={faqs}
>
	<h2>The short version</h2>
	<p>
		JSON Beam is a <strong>100% client-side</strong> JSON workbench. The JSON you paste,
		type, or open is processed entirely inside your own browser and is
		<strong>never uploaded, logged, transmitted, sold, or shared</strong>. We do not run a
		server that receives your data, we do not require an account, and we do not use tracking
		cookies. This page explains, in plain language, exactly what that means.
	</p>

	<h2>1. The data you process stays on your device</h2>
	<p>
		Formatting, validating, repairing, querying, comparing, visualizing, and converting all
		happen locally, on your machine, using JavaScript that runs in your browser. When you
		<a href="/json-formatter">format JSON</a>, <a href="/json-validator">validate it</a>, or
		<a href="/json-diff">compare two documents</a>, that content is never sent anywhere. There
		is no upload step, no API call carrying your payload, and no copy kept on our side —
		because there is no “our side” in the loop. This is why you can safely work with
		API keys, customer records, access tokens, and proprietary configuration files.
	</p>

	<h2>2. Information stored locally in your browser</h2>
	<p>
		To remember your preferences between visits, we store a small amount of data in your
		browser’s <code>localStorage</code> — for example, whether you prefer the light or
		dark editor theme (the <code>jb-theme</code> key). This data:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>lives only in your browser on your device;</li>
		<li>is never transmitted to us or any third party;</li>
		<li>can be cleared at any time by clearing your site data in your browser.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>3. Information collected automatically</h2>
	<p>
		Like virtually every website, the static files that make up JSON Beam are delivered by a
		hosting and content-delivery provider. When your browser requests those files, the provider
		may automatically process standard technical request metadata — such as your IP
		address, browser type, and the time of the request — to deliver the page, keep the
		service secure, and prevent abuse. This is ordinary web-server information, it is not linked
		to the JSON you process, and it never includes the content of your documents.
	</p>

	<h2>4. Cookies and tracking</h2>
	<p>
		We do not use advertising cookies or cross-site tracking, and we do not build profiles of
		our users. We currently do not run third-party analytics. If we ever introduce analytics, we
		will favor privacy-respecting, aggregate measurement and disclose it here before turning it
		on.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
	<p>
		Our only essential third party is the hosting/CDN provider that serves the site’s static
		files, as described above. We self-host our fonts, so no external font network requests are
		made. We do not embed third-party trackers or share data with advertisers. Should this
		change — for example, if we add optional, non-tracking ads to keep the tools free —
		we will update this policy, and the content you process will remain on your device.
	</p>
	<p>
		If — and only if — you choose to send us a message through our
		<a href="/contact">contact form</a>, that message is delivered to us by email through
		Web3Forms, a third-party form-to-email provider. Web3Forms processes the details you enter
		(such as your name, email address, and message) solely to deliver them to us. We receive only
		what you type, and only when you press Send; we use it to reply to you, and we do not sell or
		share it. Using the form is entirely optional — it exists only so you can reach us
		without our having to publish an email address.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Data security</h2>
	<p>
		The most effective security measure is architectural: because your data never leaves your
		browser, there is no central store of user JSON to breach, leak, or subpoena. The site is
		served over HTTPS so the application files reach you intact and untampered.
	</p>

	<h2>7. Children’s privacy</h2>
	<p>
		JSON Beam is a general-purpose developer tool and is not directed at children. We do not
		knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13.
	</p>

	<h2>8. Your rights</h2>
	<p>
		Because we do not collect or store personal data about you, there is no profile to access,
		correct, export, or delete on our servers. You remain in full control of the JSON you work
		with and of the preferences stored in your own browser, which you can clear at any time. If
		you have a question about your rights under a law such as the GDPR or CCPA, contact us using
		the details below.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>
		We may update this policy as the product evolves — for instance, if we add new features
		or services. When we do, we will revise the “Last updated” date at the top of this
		page. Material changes will be made clear. Our core commitment will not change: the content
		you process stays private to you.
	</p>

	<h2>10. Contact us</h2>
	<p>
		If you have any questions about this privacy policy or how JSON Beam handles data, send us a
		message through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
	</p>
</ContentPage>
